#set text(8.6pt)

#H[1 · The air system v4 · the malqaf at L5 (no HRV)]
- *One tower* at the courtyard's north-west corner (an RC core, the foot chamber 1.2 × 1.97 m clear on the ground floor, the shaft 1.35 × 0.8 clear, the head above the roof at +13.20) with *two completely separate air paths*.
- *Path (a), the courtyard breeze (natural, no fan):* the head's north face mesh and flaps → damper *D1* at the shaft's head → the shaft → the *dust trap* in the chamber (a GRP tray, a trapped gully with a primer) → damper *D2* → the *outlet louvres* 1.4 × 1.0 at +0.60 … +1.60 in the first arcade arch, fixed 15° south-east onto the olive and the water trough. Estimate ≈ 1.8 m³/s at the summer-evening mean wind (21 km/h at the mast); to be confirmed (a CFD or wind-tunnel check if wanted). *D4:* a passive gravity louvre Ø160 from the chamber to the outlet so the chamber never stays damp. An optional mobile evaporative cooler has its space in the chamber.
- *Path (b), the house's fresh air (filtered, never stops):* a downward hood under the head's south overhang (+7.6, a bird mesh, never closes) → a Ø315 duct down the chamber's south-east corner → a washable ISO Coarse 60 % pre-filter + an ISO ePM1 ≥ 50 % (F7 class) fine filter, a mechanical gauge → a quiet *EC fan 750 m³/h at 250 Pa* (≈ 160 W) on anti-vibration mounts → a 0.9 m lined silencer → a sealed Ø250 riser in the shaft's west side → high grilles (+6.4) into the family living and the gallery, and at the ground floor (+2.7) into the riwaq and the women's majlis; the other rooms through the open plan, 15 mm door undercuts or transfer grilles. *No bedroom is ducted from the core.* ASHRAE 62.2 gives ≈ 330 m³/h normal and ≈ 705 m³/h boost with the men's majlis full (24 guests); to confirm against SBC 501 / 1101.
- *Positive pressure* ≈ +5–10 Pa (the supply over the continuous extracts ≈ 150–250 m³/h of the bathrooms and the dryer); the house tight. *The kitchen hood* (600–1 000 m³/h) exceeds the fan: *its interlocked, filtered, motorised make-up inlet (≈ 300 m³/h, opens with the hood) is mandatory* (owner). Winter: the breeze closed, ≈ 1.1 kW of heat at 10 K, no heat recovery.
- *Controls, simple (owner, 9 Nov 2026): two switches and a dust relay, no controller, no modes.* Switch 1 MALQAF open / closed: D1 + D2 together, insulated low-leakage blades, *spring-return closed on power loss*. Switch 2 HOUSE FAN normal / boost: two speeds set at commissioning. *The dust relay:* an outdoor PM2.5 sensor in a weather hood on the head's north face; above 50 µg/m³ for 10 min D1 and D2 close by themselves and the switch's lamp shows "dust"; they reopen below 25 µg/m³ for 30 min with the switch on; a manual override on each actuator. No D3 (the gallery grille is a sealed provision).
- *Separations* (ASHRAE 62.1 Table 5-1): the head and the inlet to the kitchen hood outlet 12.6 / 10.5 m, the east stack's vent 8.7 m, the west stack's vent *re-routed in the attic to the south-east strip* (10.1 m; no exhaust upwind of the head in the summer-evening west wind), the AC condensers in zone Z2b 3.7 m east and 2.6 m below the openings, the LPG cabinet / the grill ≈ 12 m. *Maintenance* from the chamber's carved door at ground level: the pre-filter monthly, the fine filter at 200 Pa (≈ 6 months), the dust trap, the gully, the dampers yearly.
- *Open:* the engineer sizes the fan, the filters, the silencer, D1 / D2 and the relay, the louvres and grilles, the make-up inlet, the vent re-route, the chamber's gully and electrics; the on-site weather station before the head is detailed.

#H[2 · Cooling and heating · inverter split units per zone (owner's direction)]
- *AC by inverter split units, one per zone* (no central plant): the men's majlis (the units not over the seats, R-12), the women's majlis, the living / dining (the normal-height dining half is the conditioned one; the double-height living opens to the courtyard), the kitchen, the family lobby, the maid's wing; on the first floor the bedrooms, the kids' room, the family living, the suite, the office, the gym. *The condensers in zone Z2b on the roof* behind the cut / east attic wall (on pads, ≈ 1.0 kN each, out of sight and downwind of the head); their *condensate by tundishes / trapped air-breaks* to the east stack (never direct).
- *Drop beams in finished rooms are hidden by gypsum ceilings that also carry the AC and the lighting* (the rule since V6.2); the indoor units and routes to be coordinated with those ceilings and the beam soffits (+3.05 … +3.20 before finishes).
- *Heating:* the winter fresh air is not recovered (≈ 1.1 kW); the splits heat the rooms; the suite court is the family's winter sun room (no heating).
- *Open:* the zoning, the unit sizes and the refrigerant routes to Z2b; the electrical load (the PV / battery provision below).

#H[3 · Drainage · the stacks and the foul route]
- *West:* the *west shaft* (x 0–1.5 × y 9.2–10.4, in the utility room, doors on each floor) takes the family WC's wall-hung WC and basin (first floor); the ground-floor wash block (the powder room, the guest WC, the guest basins, the hospitality kitchen, the utility room's drip tray) on the *buried west run* under the block; the malqaf chamber's gully west to the same run. Its vent to the roof re-routed to the south-east strip.
- *X3 (new, 15 Nov 2026):* the twin bedrooms' baths back to back at y 14.125–15.525: both wall-hung WCs on the shared wet wall x 2.10 into *one stack at (2.10, 15.23)* dropping straight into the ground-floor powder room's WC compartment (y 14.55–16.1) and on to the west run; the two showers and the two basins in the floor build-up to it (≤ 2 m each). The old bedroom 3 bath stack over the ground-floor family WC is removed.
- *East:* the *stack outside the east wall at y 7.05 behind a removable cladding panel* (the owner's choice over an internal duct, 3 Nov 2026): the suite bath (the shower on its north wall over the stack, the two basins on the east wall with their wastes north of the hood zone, the tub), the suite's WC closet, *bedroom 1's bath* (its shower back to back with the suite's), the AC condensate; four branch fittings at +3.4 … +3.9, a rodding eye, the vent ≥ 3 m from the filtered inlet. *No drain over the kitchen hood* (x 12.4–13.311, y 10.1–11.3). The kitchen extract through the east wall south of the service door.
- *The maid bath and the east block:* the maid bath (east of the maid room under the step's wall, 17 Nov 2026) drains *straight out through the east wall*; with the kitchen and the laundry (the washers, the dryer, the utility sink, a floor drain) they run to the *east-yard foul chamber* (14.3, 13.5), which never takes rain.
- *The foul route:* both clusters → inspection chambers → north and west to the *existing septic outside the north wall near corner C1* (it serves the old house too; its inlet level, capacity and condition unknown: a pump station at the gate's collector chamber if the inlet is too high); a chamber at every change of direction (owner). *Everywhere:* deep-seal traps ≥ 75 mm, anti-odour floor drains, *automatic trap primers on the rarely used drains*, acoustic (triple-layer) pipes on every stack, cleanouts, two real vent stacks to the roof.

#H[4 · Rain · the courtyard, the suite court and the roof (never joined to the foul system)]
- *The courtyard:* the whole floor level with gentle falls to *two linear drains and an overflow*, the water trough's drain and the olive pot's saucer pipe, east under the kitchen floor (a cleanout at the kitchen's west wall) to its *own rain chamber* (15.7, 18.1) in the east yard → the east soakaway.
- *The suite court:* the floor falls south at 1.5 % to a box gutter along the south side with an overflow spout through the south wall; linear slot drains in front of the three doors (near-flush thresholds); the membrane turned up ≥ 150 mm; the structural slab depressed 0.10–0.15.
- *The roof:* 11 outlets → internal downpipes in the walls (the rain points N, W ×2, E, cut, S ×2) → the rain chambers → *two soakaways* (east and south: ≥ 5 m from the walls, ≥ 1 m inside the deed line, ≥ 10 m from the well, assumed rules) with overflows; the malqaf head's roof included.

#H[5 · Water supply · the heaters west and east]
- *Supply:* tankers to the existing ground tank south-west of the old house (3 × 2.5 assumed) and a reserved place for a new tank; a roof tank between the roof beams R10 – R3 (up to 30 kN allowed in the structure); the pumps; the water pipe ≥ 1.5 m from the drains along the driveway. *The water system study is still open* (the tanks, the roof tank, the pumps, the filter).
- *Inside:* a *manifold system* (one continuous PEX pipe from the manifold to each fixture, no buried joints) with a *manifold cabinet per floor near each shaft* (west: the utility room GF, the family WC's wall FF; east: the laundry GF, the suite closet's wall FF) and a valve per fixture; *two heaters:* west ≈ 100–120 L in the utility room (on a drip tray with a leak sensor, 1 m from the battery cabinet), east ≈ 150 L in the laundry, or a central heat-pump unit on the roof with a ring main if the engineer prefers; *leak sensors* under the heaters, the washer, the dishwasher and every basin cabinet wired to an *automatic main shut-off valve* after the filter.

#H[6 · Greywater · from the first floor only (owner's direction, 17 Nov 2026)]
- *The first floor's greywater only* (the showers, basins and tubs of the four first-floor baths and the family WC's basin) is collected *separately and goes straight to the farm's irrigation* (the south garden, diversion chambers to the foul line when needed); *nothing from the ground floor* (the kitchen, the laundry, the ground-floor basins and the guest side stay on the foul route to the septic). The WCs of both floors are black water to the septic.
- *What it means:* a second (grey) pipe beside each foul stack: in the west shaft, on the wet wall x 2.10 (the X3 pair), behind the east cladding panel; grey branches kept apart from the WC branches in the first-floor floor build-ups; a diversion chamber with a filter before the garden; the municipality's position on greywater reuse to be asked. *To size and route by the engineer.*

#H[7 · Electrical, briefly]
- The main panel, the manifold, the heater and the *inverter and battery cabinet* in the utility room (west, away from the water; the space and ventilation to confirm); the *PV provision* on the roof (the zones free of shade, fixing points before the waterproofing, conduits to the panel); *no generator* (the backup from the PV and batteries when installed). *Fire safety at home level:* interconnected mains smoke alarms with battery back-up in every bedroom, outside each sleeping area and on every floor, a heat alarm in the kitchen, gas and CO detectors; low-level night lights on the bedroom routes; the malqaf's two switches and the dust relay; the lift (two stops) by the supplier.

#H[8 · Open questions for the engineer and the owner]
+ *Sizes and routes* of everything above: the fan, the filters, the dampers and the relay, the AC zones and the condensers in Z2b, the stacks and the falls, the pump station if the septic's inlet is high, the soakaways (with the soil report), the tanks and pumps, the heaters' type, the greywater line and its diversion chambers.
+ *The survey and the levels:* the septic's inlet level and condition, the street level at the gate, the farm's levels; the drainage falls re-checked.
+ *The municipality:* the septic's reuse and its position outside the wall, the rain soakaways, greywater reuse, the gas cabinet, Civil Defense's villa requirements.
+ *The kitchen hood* route and its make-up inlet; the dryer's exhaust; the bathrooms' extracts (ducted fans in the suite closet, bath 3, the family WC, the powder room compartment).
+ *The lengthening* of ≈ 0.95 m (the twin bedrooms' 4.0 m rooms) is still open with the owner: the garden's chambers and the south soakaway (3.75 m from the south wall today, to be moved to keep 5 m) move with it.
